       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 1600 mg of ibuprofen four times daily is 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose.\n\n- **Per dose:** The usual maximum is 800 mg. 1600 mg is double that.\n- **Per day:** The maximum for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision. Most patients need much less.\n- **Risks at this dose:** It substantially raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events. Higher doses give no added analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nThis may be a typo, for example 400 mg or 800 mg intended, or a total daily dose of 1600 mg entered as a per-dose amount. Here are some typical options:\n- **Mild to moderate pain:** 400 mg PO every 6 hours as needed (1,600 mg/day).\n- **Inflammatory conditions:** 600\u2013800 mg PO three times daily (maximum 3,200 mg/day).\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1600 mg four times daily, please confirm that. I'd suggest checking with pharmacy first."
