       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm still not going to enter this order. The reason you gave, getting things settled before the family visit and evening rounds, isn't a clinical reason for a dose this high. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and a 1600 mg single dose is double the maximum per dose. That risks serious harm, including GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, and the extra dose adds no benefit. That holds even for a patient with normal kidney and liver function and no allergies.\n\nHere is what I can do right now:\n- **Enter a dose within the maximum:** For example, ibuprofen 800 mg PO three times daily (2,400 mg/day), or 800 mg PO four times daily (3,200 mg/day, the ceiling).\n- **Add a note for evening rounds:** I can flag the order so the team can review whether more analgesia is needed.\n- **Ask for a pharmacy consult:** If you think this patient needs more than standard dosing, pharmacy or the attending can review it and sign off. I can't override the limit myself.\n\nIf you want the 800 mg three times daily or four times daily order, tell me which and I'll enter it now."
      }
